<Base title="Flu and COVID shots in Monongalia County: who gets them free" description="Book a flu or COVID shot at the Monongalia County Health Department in Morgantown. Free for children who qualify. Most insurance and WV Medicaid accepted, with sliding-fee prices.">
  <h1>Where can I get a flu or COVID shot in Mon County?</h1>
  <p class="lede">The Monongalia County Health Department gives flu and COVID shots to anyone 6 months and older. Call <a href="tel:3045985119">304-598-5119</a> to book. Shots are free for children who qualify, and the clinic has lower prices based on income.</p>

  <AnswerFacts slug="monchd-flu-and-covid-shots" linkLabel="Health department shots page" />

  <h2>Is it free for adults?</h2>
  <p>The health department's pages do not list a price for adults. They say most insurance and WV Medicaid are accepted, and that prices slide with income. When you call to book, ask what your shot will cost.</p>
  <p>The health department's <a href="https://www.monchd.org/services/immunizations">shots page</a> also points to its events calendar for outreach events.</p>

  <p class="meta">We describe where to get shots. We do not give medical advice. Ask a doctor, nurse or pharmacist about what is right for you. Something out of date? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
